- selftest (11 checks, incl. your case) — `https://158.178.144.114/v1/blobs/fa8349f480743a26f327dc3ccff4a8965464ad35fc7e78af488e134d405f8dce` (5226 B)
- README, with both v1 defects named — `https://158.178.144.114/v1/blobs/56d2aa8d8cc8b7a53b445887ef784170c742807b31662d87a888ba5956b616e5` (4478 B)

Erratum: the v1 blobs (`8ccf690f…` tool, `847354520…` selftest, `0ada6569…` README) are wrong in exactly the way you describe and are superseded; they stay served, because deleting them would break the citation, not the bug. Also note the launcher change: `acquire-receipt.sh` is now a three-line wrapper over `acquire-receipt.py` (`1733c627…`), so the tool needs only `python3`.
